</div>

<div class="key-takeaways-section" id="key-takeaways">
  <div class="page-width">
    <div class="section-heading page-width-inner">
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="st-row key-takeaway__items">
      <div class="st-col-md-3 st-col-6 key-takeaway__item">
        <div class="box">
          <div class="ico-holder">
            <img src="{{ 'icon-battery-charging.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="icons">
          </div>
          <p>Use a thicker gauge (lower AWG) for longer cords to prevent power loss</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="st-col-md-3 st-col-6 key-takeaway__item">
        <div class="box">
          <div class="ico-holder">
            <img src="{{ 'icon-plug-zap.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="icons">
          </div>
          <p>For high-power devices (heaters, power tools, A/C units), use <strong>12 AWG or lower</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="st-col-md-3 st-col-6 key-takeaway__item">
        <div class="box">
          <div class="ico-holder">
            <img src="{{ 'icon-lightbulb.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="icons">
          </div>
          <p><strong>Never daisy-chain</strong> multiple extension cords — this increases resistance and fire risks</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="st-col-md-3 st-col-6 key-takeaway__item">
        <div class="box">
          <div class="ico-holder">
            <img src="{{ 'icon-link-off.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="icons">
          </div>
          <p>Use a thicker gauge (lower AWG) for longer cords to prevent power loss</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="usage-guidelines" id="usage-guidelines">
  <div class="page-width">
    <div class="safe-usage-guidelines-description gutters-end-0">
      <h2>Safe Usage Guidelines</h2>
      <h3>Do Not Overload</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Check the wattage rating of the cord and never exceed it.</li>
        <li>
          Plug high-power appliances (heaters, air conditioners) directly into a wall outlet rather than an extension
          cord.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Avoid Daisy-Chaining</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Never connect multiple extension cords together — this increases resistance and risk of fire.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Keep Cords in Good Condition</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Inspect cords for frays, cracks, or exposed wires before each use.</li>
        <li>Do not run cords under rugs, carpets, or furniture, as this can trap heat and cause overheating.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Unplug When Not in Use</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Reduce energy waste and prevent overheating by unplugging cords when not in use.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="important-warning-description gutters-end-0">
      <h2>Important <strong>Outdoor Use Warning</strong></h2>
      <p>
        Even if an extension cord is labeled for outdoor use (e.g., <strong>SJTW</strong>, <strong>STW</strong>, or
        <strong>SPT</strong> with an outdoor rating), that rating only applies to the
        <strong>insulation and jacket</strong> — meaning it can withstand moisture, sunlight, and temperature changes.
      </p>
      <p>
        However, the <strong>plug itself is not waterproof</strong> unless specifically designed to be. You should
        always avoid exposing the plug or outlet connection to water, as this can cause
        <strong>electrical shock, short circuits, or equipment damage.</strong> When used outdoors, always protect plug
        connections with proper weatherproof covers or enclosures.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="key-safety-points-description gutters-end-0">
      <h2>Summary of Key Safety Points</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Always select cords certified by <strong>UL</strong>, <strong>ETL</strong>, or <strong>CSA</strong></li>
        <li>
          Match <strong>gauge (AWG)</strong> and <strong>length</strong> to the power requirements of your devices
        </li>
        <li>Follow <strong>NEC</strong> and <strong>NEMA</strong> standards for installation and usage</li>
        <li>Keep cords dry, undamaged, and unplugged when not in use.</li>
        <li>
          Proper selection and safe use of extension cords ensure both <strong>performance and protection</strong> for
          your home, workspace, or job site.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  // Container selector
  const tabContainer = document.querySelector('.extension-cord-tabs');

  if (tabContainer) {
    const tabButtons = tabContainer.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn');
    const tabItems = tabContainer.querySelectorAll('.tab-item');

    tabButtons.forEach((btn) => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const targetTab = btn.getAttribute('data-tab');

        // Remove active class from buttons
        tabButtons.forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
        btn.classList.add('active');

        // Remove active/show classes from tab items
        tabItems.forEach((tab) => {
          tab.classList.remove('active', 'show');
        });

        // Add active to target tab
        const target = tabContainer.querySelector('#' + targetTab);
        target.classList.add('active');

        // small timeout for smooth fade
        setTimeout(() => {
          target.classList.add('show');
        }, 10);
      });
    });
  }
</script>

